<title>NETHERLANDS: ROYAL DUTCH MOVES HIGHER AT MIDDAY.</title>
<headline>ROYAL DUTCH MOVES HIGHER AT MIDDAY.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Royal Dutch built on early light gains by midday on Monday, trading 3.20 guilders up at 285.40 amid a generally weaker Amsterdam bourse after weekend reports it was planning a bid for British Gas .</p>
<p>The companies declined to comment on the report in Britain's Sunday Telegraph which said the Anglo-Dutch oil giant had approached British Gas with plans for a 40 billion stg merger.</p>
<p>But dealers in Amsterdam on Monday remained sceptical.</p>
<p>&quot;People are treating it strictly as a rumour but there is some buying coming into the stock -- that could be originating from London,&quot; one said. -- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
